      "writtenOn": "2022-04-05T12:10:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "re second point: My point is that what we really want is a check that tells whether the module that I am building can safely run on platforms newer than X or not. That\u0027s what min_sdk_version is for. sdk_version just specifies the stub library that will be in the classpath.\n\nFurthermore, the current check is sometimes too restrictive, and sometimes too permissive. For example, checkSdkLinkType disallows (linktype: current) -\u003e (linktype: private_api), but allows (linktype: system_30) -\u003e (linktype: system_31), because it doesn\u0027t distinguish the different versions of the same API surface. Actually, (linktype: system_30) -\u003e (linktype: system_31) should be allowed if min_sdk_version \u003e\u003d 31, but be disallowed if min_sdk_version \u003c 31. The check based on simple comparison of rank [1] can\u0027t determine such cases.\n\n[1] https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/+/master:build/soong/java/base.go;drc\u003dec198caf7e1e6e4bea5a891e399d18a6c4f917ec;l\u003d1830",
